# Line endings
#
# Every blob in this repository is already stored with LF, but Windows clones
# default to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites the working tree to CRLF on
# checkout. Biome then reads CRLF and reports a formatting error on every line
# of every file, so `npm run quality:v1` fails locally for reasons that have
# nothing to do with the change under review - while CI, on Linux, passes.
#
# `eol=lf` pins the working tree to LF regardless of a developer's autocrlf
# setting. Because the stored blobs are already LF, this needs no renormalising
# commit: it only changes what lands on disk at checkout.
#
# After pulling this file for the first time, refresh an existing checkout:
#
#   git rm --cached -r . && git reset --hard
#
# (Commit or stash your work first - `reset --hard` discards uncommitted
# changes.) A fresh clone needs nothing.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files, which must never be line-ending converted or diffed as text.
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.png   binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.wasm  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary

# Generated. Collapsed in diffs so a dependency bump does not bury a review.
package-lock.json  linguist-generated=true -diff
bun.lock           linguist-generated=true -diff
